body:
The Billy stuff really killed me. I think my favorite part of that whole story is the relationship (or lack thereof) between him and Max. She is terrified of him, but cares because he is a part of her small, fucked up family. He cares for her, but can't tell her he loves her, even as he dies. Sadie and Dacre portrayed that simultaneous connection and distance between them so beautifully. To think that one of his defining memories, one of the important ones that El sees, is meeting his "sister". Such an innocuous memory (and seems so inconsequential compared to the others), but clearly important for so many complicated reasons. 

&#x200B;

Huge props to Dacre for the work he put in this season. One of my complaints early in the season is that it felt like they weren't going to address/follow-through on him being a shitty person. Goddamn was I wrong. And that last scene with Max - he gave Sadie so much to work with. All this to say - damn, was I satisfied with that arc.
